---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Getting to the Water"
  description="MBR City's water features — District One's Crystal Lagoon and the Riviera canal — versus the honest drive time to an actual Dubai beach."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Getting to the water</p>
    <h1>Lagoon and canal, sea by car</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      MBR City has two genuinely distinctive water features of its own —
      neither of them is the sea, and this page exists for the same reason
      Riviera's does: to separate the marketing imagery from what's actually
      true about getting to the coast.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>District One's Crystal Lagoon</h2>
    <p>
      A large artificial lagoon with clear turquoise water, ringed by a
      running and cycling track — the closest thing MBR City has to a
      beach-like amenity, and open to residents of the surrounding villas
      rather than the district as a whole. It's a real, well-regarded
      feature, just not a substitute for the sea if that's specifically
      what you're after.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The Riviera canal</h2>
    <p>
      The Dubai Water Canal runs along Azizi Riviera specifically, with its
      own walkway and water taxi connections toward Business Bay and
      Downtown. Covered in full, including the honest canal-versus-beach
      distinction, on <a href="https://riviera.dst.llc/getting-to-the-water/">Riviera's own page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Reaching an actual beach</h2>
    <p>
      From most points in MBR City, the nearest public beaches — Kite
      Beach, La Mer, and JBR — are a 20–30 minute drive, similar regardless
      of which community you're in, since the district as a whole sits a
      comparable distance from the coast. There's no direct transit link
      from MBR City to the beach; a car or taxi is the realistic option.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: var(--space-5); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
